[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Famous Monastery]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.54]Lesson 8 | 第8课
[00:02.15]A famous monastery | 著名的修道院
[00:09.49]What are the St.Bernard dogs used for? | 圣伯纳德犬是用来干什么的？
[00:15.03]The Great St.Bernard Pass connects Switzerland to Italy. | 圣伯纳德大山口连接着瑞士与意大利。
[00:20.49]At 2,473 metres, it is the highest mountain pass in Europe. | 它海拔2473米，是欧洲最高的山口。
[00:28.15]The famous monastery of St.Bernard, | 著名的圣伯纳德修道院
[00:31.71]which was founded in the eleventh century, lies about a mile away. | 建于11世纪，坐落在离山口一英里的地方。
[00:36.95]For hundreds of years, St.Bernard dogs have saved the lives of travellers crossing the dangerous Pass. | 几百年来，圣伯纳德犬拯救了穿越危险山口的旅行者的性命。
[00:44.64]These friendly dogs, which were first brought from Asia, | 这些最先从亚洲引进的友善的狗，
[00:49.20]were used as watchdogs even in Roman times. | 早在罗马时代就给人当看门狗了。
[00:53.39]Now that a tunnel has been built through the mountains, the Pass is less dangerous, | 如今由于在山里开通了隧道，山口不那么危险了，
[00:58.92]but each year, the dogs are still sent out into the snow whenever a traveller is in difficulty. | 但每年一旦有旅行者陷入困境，这些狗仍会被派到雪地里去。
[01:06.32]Despite the new tunnel, | 尽管修了新的隧道，
[01:07.93]there are still a few people who rashly attempt to cross the Pass on foot. | 仍有一些人莽撞地企图徒步跨越山口。
[01:14.69]During the summer months, the monastery is very busy, | 夏季的几个月里，修道院十分繁忙，
[01:18.30]for it is visited by thousands of people who cross the Pass in cars. | 因为成千上万的人乘车穿过山口来此参观。
[01:24.01]As there are so many people about, the dogs have to be kept in a special enclosure. | 由于周围人太多，这些狗只得被关在专门的围栏里。
[01:30.32]In winter, however, life at the monastery is quite different. | 然而到了冬天，修道院里的生活则完全不同了。
[01:35.72]The temperature drops to -30 degrees, | 气温下降到零下30度，
[01:38.73]and very few people attempt to cross the Pass. | 几乎没有人企图跨越山口。
[01:42.74]The monks prefer winter to summer for they have more privacy. | 修道士们喜欢冬天胜过夏天，因为冬天他们更清静。
[01:47.68]The dogs have greater freedom, too, | 狗也比较自由，
[01:50.39]for they are allowed to wander outside their enclosure. | 因为允许它们在围栏外四处走动。
[01:53.92]The only regular visitors to the monastery in winter are parties of skiers who go there at Christmas and Easter. | 冬天经常来修道院参观的只有一批批滑雪者，他们在圣诞节和复活节去那里。
[02:02.36]These young people, | 这些年轻人
[02:04.34]who love the peace of the mountains, | 热爱山中的宁静，
[02:06.56]always receive a warm welcome at St.Bernard's monastery. | 在圣伯纳德修道院总是受到热烈欢迎。
